# Every build- or host-dependent lit feature goes through build_feature()
# in test/lit.cfg.py, so a test that needs a feature this build lacks is
# left out of collection instead of showing as UNSUPPORTED. A direct
# config.available_features.add() of a new feature would bring the
# UNSUPPORTED line back; the only direct calls allowed are the helper's
# own and disabled-test (which shows as UNSUPPORTED on purpose).
RUN: grep 'available_features\.add(' %S/../lit.cfg.py | not grep -v -e '^#' -e 'add(name)$' -e 'add("disabled-test")$'

